{"name":"Biscay","hex":"#2f3c53","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Biscay","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A province of the Basque Country, Spain.","Ellipsis of Bay of Biscay."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Biscay"}],"entries":[{"title":"Biscay","blocks":[{"text":"The Province of Biscay is a province of the Basque Autonomous Community, heir of the ancient Lordship of Biscay, lying on the south shore of the eponymous bay. The capital and largest city is Bilbao."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Biscay_in_Spain_%28plus_Canarias%29.svg/330px-Biscay_in_Spain_%28plus_Canarias%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biscay","wikidata":"Q93366"},{"title":"Biscay (Congress of Deputies constituency)","blocks":[{"text":"Biscay is one of the 52 constituencies represented in the Congress of Deputies, the lower chamber of the Spanish parliament, the Cortes Generales. The constituency currently elects eight deputies. The electoral system uses the D'Hondt method and closed-list proportional voting, with a minimum threshold of three percent."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/05/SpanishCongressDistricts%28Biscay%29.png/330px-SpanishCongressDistricts%28Biscay%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biscay_(Congress_of_Deputies_constituency)","wikidata":"Q4917218"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Santimamine-Santimami%C3%B1e.JPG/500px-Santimamine-Santimami%C3%B1e.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/08/Santimamine-Santimami%C3%B1e.JPG/1280px-Santimamine-Santimami%C3%B1e.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wi